; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Triangle Family
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     triangle, angles, repeat, setxy
; SUMMARY:  Draws an equilateral triangle, a right triangle, a tall thin triangle and a stack of triangles.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Four kinds of triangle appear across the screen. The last one
;   is a little tower of triangles stacked like a pyramid of cups.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Try typing  tri 150  in the command center.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * why the turtle turns 120 degrees, not 60, for an equilateral triangle
;   * using SETXY to close a shape exactly, without working out the last side
;   * POS remembers where the turtle is so it can come back
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Turn 60 instead of 120 in TRI. Why does the shape not close?
;   * Change the height in TALLTRIANGLE to 250.
;   * Give PYRAMID 5 rows instead of 4.
; ============================================================

; The inside corner of an equilateral triangle is 60 degrees, but the
; turtle turns the OUTSIDE angle: it must swing round 180 - 60 = 120
; degrees to walk along the next side. Three turns of 120 make 360.
to tri :size
  repeat 3 [forward :size right 120]
end

; A right triangle: walk up, turn a square corner, walk across,
; then SETXY straight back to the start. The computer works out
; the long slanted side for us.
to righttriangle :up :across
  localmake "start pos
  forward :up
  right 90
  forward :across
  setxy first :start last :start
  setheading 0
end

; A tall isosceles triangle. We visit the three corners by
; their coordinates, measured from the start (the bottom left).
to talltriangle :width :height
  localmake "x xcor
  localmake "y ycor
  setxy :x + :width / 2 :y + :height
  setxy :x + :width :y
  setxy :x :y
end

; A pyramid of triangles: 1 on top, then 2, then 3 ...
; Each row starts half a triangle further left and one row lower.
to pyramid :rows :size
  localmake "h :size * (sqrt 3) / 2
  for [row 1 :rows] [
    for [k 1 :row] [
      setpencolor 9 + remainder :row + :k 6
      right 30 tri :size left 30
      penup right 90 forward :size left 90 pendown
    ]
    ; back to the start of this row, then down and left for the next row
    penup
    left 90 forward :size * :row right 90
    back :h
    left 90 forward :size / 2 right 90
    pendown
  ]
end

to jumpto :x :y
  penup setxy :x :y setheading 0 pendown
end

clearscreen
setpensize 3

jumpto -340 -60
setpencolor 1
right 30 tri 150 left 30

jumpto -150 -60
setpencolor 4
righttriangle 170 120

jumpto 0 -120
setpencolor 2
talltriangle 100 280

jumpto 210 100
pyramid 4 60
hideturtle
